  "notes": "At a Hi-Fi show, we often talk about resolution, dynamics, realism and soundstage — but rarely about the actual level at which those qualities are being demonstrated.\nThis measurement, taken during a listening session at the HiFi Stereo NET Show at Heathrow, looks at the SPL behind the experience. A system may sound effortless and refined even at a high level, which can make the true exposure less obvious than with harsher or more distorted playback.\nThat makes the question interesting: does better sound quality make loud listening feel more comfortable — and therefore easier to underestimate?\nA small real-world measurement linking perceived quality, playback level and listening exposure.\nCurtesy Airt",
